 "scope": "Level 1. Area 1 The Crumbling Coast and Area 2 The Bridge Ambush, as one continuous course. Area 3 The Archway Boss is not built yet.",
 "tagline": "The ground is coming apart.",
 "brief": "Cross the breaking coast, hold the bridge, climb the broken isles.",
 "note": "Opening rebuilt to the Magic Cliffs demo scene: mesa (tree at the left) -> bridge -> mesa -> a jumped chasm -> the pierced archway rock, which meets the original course at x1452. The hanging stalactite and the archway mass are rock_mass set dressing (features/world/scenery.gd), not collision. Flat grass line y648. Everything from x1452 on is the original course.",
 "solids_note": "The optional fifth value names the art the rectangle wears. Without one it is a grassed cliff; with one it is that piece, centred and sitting on the top edge. Collision is the rectangle either way.",
 "hazards_note": "Deliberately none. The Fractured Isles kills by the fall, not by spikes: every threat here is a gap you misjudged or a bandit who reached you. Spikes are instant death regardless of health, which would undercut the health-bar fight the level is built around.",
 "decor_note": "[x, y, piece] with the piece's bottom edge at y and x its centre. Plants stand on a surface; vine and vine_rock hang DOWN a cliff face, so their y is below the lip and their own dark backing is kept because it matches the rock. Art only, never collision. scripts/check_levels.py warns if a standing plant is left hanging.",
 "enemies_note": "Two on the deck and one waiting on the far side, so the crossing is fought from both directions. A blast staggers whichever is closer. A fourth value \"perch\" marks an enemy that does NOT hold its section's gate: the six on the high ledges cannot be reached on foot and the blast flies flat, so a gate that waited for them could never open. They are harassment, not a lock.",
 "gates": [
  2240,
  4460,
  6110
 ],
 "gates_note": "The x of each section's end wall. Three gates make four sections, and the fourth has none: it is the Archway boss platform, which the flag ends instead. A gate is shut while any enemy in its section still holds it, and while it is shut the camera stops with it at the right edge of the screen and an invisible wall stands on the line - you have run out of screen, not out of floor. Clearing the section opens both. Walking back is never blocked. Positions are chokepoints read off the level's own geometry: 2240 is the lip before the first crossing, 4460 the end of the long bridge's floor, 6110 the last of the deep isles before the hops to the Archway.",
 "music": "magic_cliffs",
 "music_note": "A file in godot/audio/ without its extension, played for as long as the level is. Omit it and the level is silent - both greybox slices are. The Fractured Isles and the title screen name the same loop, which is the one the Magic Cliffs pack ships, so starting a new journey carries straight on from the menu rather than restarting the track."
}
